LC 205 — Isomorphic Strings
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:
Each character in s must always map to one character in t.

Example:
egg → add

e → a
g → d

Mapping is consistent ✅

Algorithm:
Create mapping s → t
Create mapping t → s

For each character:
    if mapping conflicts → false
    store both mappings

return true

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    bool isIsomorphic(string s, string t) {
        int mp1[256] = {}, mp2[256] = {};

        for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {
            if (mp1[s[i]] != mp2[t[i]])
                return false;

            mp1[s[i]] = i + 1;
            mp2[t[i]] = i + 1;
        }

        return true;
    }
};


EX:
s = "egg"
t = "add"

e → a ✅
g → d ✅
g → d ✅

Answer = true ✅
